WEBVTT

00:13:28.375 --> 00:13:30.976
I think we sometimes learn new things

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:33.601
when our assumptions are
tested and questioned.

00:13:33.625 --> 00:13:35.684
And so the idea that you can say something

00:13:35.708 --> 00:13:38.559
and then I can disagree with it
and decide that I was wrong

00:13:38.583 --> 00:13:40.726
is to me a signal of learning, right?

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.434
On the other hand,
I think that one of the things I love

00:13:43.458 --> 00:13:46.184
about having a conversation with you
every time we do it

00:13:46.208 --> 00:13:48.893
is I come away with new lenses
for understanding things.

00:13:48.917 --> 00:13:51.226
They're not necessarily
correcting misconceptions

00:13:51.250 --> 00:13:53.018
or changing a belief I had,

00:13:53.042 --> 00:13:56.726
but they're giving me new ways of thinking
about the topics that I care about,

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:58.018
and I love that.

00:13:58.042 --> 00:14:00.184
So my hope is we're
going to do that tonight.